discharge|release-from-hospital|VERB|allow a patient to leave|To officially allow a patient to leave hospital care.|cho xuất viện|The hospital discharged the patient after arranging a follow-up appointment.|Bệnh viện cho người bệnh xuất viện sau khi thu xếp một cuộc hẹn tái khám.|Transitive; discharge a patient; be discharged from hospital. This does not necessarily mean fully recovered.|0
discharge|release-from-service|VERB|end military service officially|To officially allow or require someone to leave military service.|cho xuất ngũ|The navy discharged the sailor at the end of her service.|Hải quân cho nữ thủy thủ xuất ngũ khi cô kết thúc thời gian phục vụ.|Transitive; discharge someone from the armed forces. Often passive; not necessarily a punishment.|1
discharge|release-substance|VERB|send out a substance|To release a liquid or gas from a place or container.|xả; thải ra|The pipe discharges treated water into a storage tank.|Đường ống xả nước đã xử lý vào bể chứa.|Transitive or intransitive: discharge water, discharge into a tank. Discharging does not itself imply safe or unsafe quality.|2
discharge|perform-duty|VERB|carry out a duty|To carry out a duty or responsibility that you are expected to fulfil.|thực hiện nhiệm vụ hoặc nghĩa vụ|The treasurer discharged her duties with careful records and regular reports.|Người thủ quỹ thực hiện nhiệm vụ của mình bằng việc ghi chép cẩn thận và báo cáo thường xuyên.|Formal transitive use; discharge a duty or responsibility. Distinguish from being discharged from a role.|3
discharge|dismiss-from-job|VERB|end someone's employment|To require someone to leave a job or position.|cho thôi việc; miễn nhiệm|In the story, the company discharged its manager after an investigation.|Trong câu chuyện, công ty cho người quản lý thôi việc sau một cuộc điều tra.|Formal transitive use; discharge an employee; discharge someone from a post. Not the same as completing a duty.|4
hospitality|welcoming-guests|NOUN|friendly treatment of guests|Friendly and generous treatment given to visitors or guests.|lòng hiếu khách; sự tiếp đãi chu đáo|We thanked our hosts for their hospitality during the rainy weekend.|Chúng tôi cảm ơn những người chủ nhà vì sự tiếp đãi chu đáo trong cuối tuần mưa.|Uncountable; show hospitality to someone; thank someone for their hospitality.|-
layer|one-level-of-material|NOUN|one sheet or level|An amount of material covering a surface or lying above or below another amount.|lớp|A thin layer of dust covered the unused shelves.|Một lớp bụi mỏng phủ lên những kệ không được dùng.|Countable: a layer of dust; several layers. The noun does not specify a fixed thickness.|0
rope|thick-strong-cord|NOUN|thick strong cord|A strong thick cord made from strands twisted together.|dây thừng|They secured the canvas shelter with ropes before the wind strengthened.|Họ cố định mái trú bằng vải bạt bằng dây thừng trước khi gió mạnh lên.|Countable for a length or piece; uncountable as material. Tie something with rope.|0
termite|wood-feeding-insect|NOUN|wood-feeding social insect|A small insect that lives in a colony and can feed on wood.|con mối|The carpenter found termites inside the damaged wooden frame.|Người thợ mộc phát hiện mối bên trong khung gỗ bị hư hại.|Countable; a termite, termites. Termites are insects, not a kind of woodworm larva.|-
